From: Scott Tomaszewski <scottTomaszewski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 05:00:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(SC-479): a Reading-view host note keeps its scroll
 position when a tracker in a note it embeds is written

A write to note B redraws the embed of B in note A; the embed's inner sizer collapses inside one
task and Chrome scroll anchoring drives A's scrollTop to 0 (measured 2887 -> 0, Obsidian 1.15.0).
The modify listener now also pins every Reading view that shows a DSE block embedded from the
written note (host pin: sizer floor plus overflow-anchor: none for the pin's life), and the writer
pin reaches the outermost Reading scroller. A note's own pins and PIN_TTL_MS are unchanged.
Lifecycle G-S42 drives it (in-app, on disk, embed's own write with adoption off, another pane).
